From: Andrea Covelli <andcov23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH TEST-ONLY] wifi: mac80211: probe ath pre-association PTK upload

This diagnostic patch measures early PTK installation support on controlled
test devices.

During an AP-side FT roam, hostapd can install the pairwise key after the
station entry has been created but before mac80211 marks it associated.
The existing ASSOC gate returns -ENOENT before the driver's set_key()
callback runs. This experiment continues through that gate and records how
the driver and firmware handle the key at that point.

For this controlled experiment, allow a pre-association AP or AP_VLAN
pairwise key through the gate when the station exists and the hardware
advertises SW_CRYPTO_CONTROL. The in-tree drivers currently advertising this
flag are ath10k, ath11k, and ath12k. Keep the existing station-uploaded
check, call the driver's real set_key() callback, and log both the attempt
and its raw return value. EPP peers retain their existing key path.

Preserve the callback's raw return value. For a non-MLO station, a logged
return value of 0 records acceptance by the complete set_key() callback.
Classify a return value of 1 as software-crypto permission and an
inconclusive result for early hardware installation. A negative return value,
timeout, firmware failure, or broken post-roam traffic identifies an
unsupported combination of driver, firmware, hardware, and ordering.

Run this patch as the standalone replacement for the deferred-key patch.
During testing, keep one of these two patch 400 variants in the build.

Signed-off-by: Andrea Covelli <andcov23@gmail.com>
---
 net/mac80211/cfg.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 net/mac80211/key.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/cfg.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
@@ -666,7 +666,15 @@ static int ieee80211_add_key(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 		key->conf.flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_NO_AUTO_TX;
 
 	if (mac_addr) {
+		bool test_early_upload;
+
 		sta = sta_info_get_bss(sdata, mac_addr);
+		test_early_upload =
+			sta && pairwise && !sta->sta.epp_peer &&
+			!test_sta_flag(sta, WLAN_STA_ASSOC) &&
+			(sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP ||
+			 sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) &&
+			ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SW_CRYPTO_CONTROL);
 		/*
 		 * The ASSOC test makes sure the driver is ready to
 		 * receive the key. When wpa_supplicant has roamed
@@ -681,11 +689,13 @@ static int ieee80211_add_key(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 		 * If (re)association frame encryption support is not present,
 		 * cfg80211 will not allow key installation in non‑AP STA mode.
 		 *
-		 * TODO: accept the key if we have a station entry and
-		 *	 add it to the device after the station associates.
+		 * For this test only, let AP-side pairwise keys through on
+		 * SW_CRYPTO_CONTROL hardware to probe whether set_key() is
+		 * already safe before ASSOC. EPP peers retain the existing path.
 		 */
 		if (!sta || (!sta->sta.epp_peer &&
-			     !test_sta_flag(sta, WLAN_STA_ASSOC))) {
+			     !test_sta_flag(sta, WLAN_STA_ASSOC) &&
+			     !test_early_upload)) {
 			ieee80211_key_free_unused(key);
 			return -ENOENT;
 		}
--- a/net/mac80211/key.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/key.c
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ static int ieee80211_key_enable_hw_accel(struct ieee80211_key *key)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata = key->sdata;
 	struct sta_info *sta;
+	bool test_early_upload;
 	int ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	might_sleep();
@@ -148,6 +149,12 @@ static int ieee80211_key_enable_hw_accel(struct ieee80211_key *key)
 		goto out_unsupported;
 
 	sta = key->sta;
+	test_early_upload =
+		sta && (key->conf.flags & IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PAIRWISE) &&
+		!sta->sta.epp_peer && !test_sta_flag(sta, WLAN_STA_ASSOC) &&
+		(sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP ||
+		 sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) &&
+		ieee80211_hw_check(&key->local->hw, SW_CRYPTO_CONTROL);
 
 	/*
 	 * Allow installation of a per-STA GTK if per-STA GTK is supported
@@ -160,8 +167,13 @@ static int ieee80211_key_enable_hw_accel(struct ieee80211_key *key)
 	      sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN_DATA))
 		goto out_unsupported;
 
-	if (sta && !sta->uploaded)
+	if (sta && !sta->uploaded) {
+		if (test_early_upload)
+			sdata_info(sdata,
+				   "mac80211 FT key test: STA %pM not uploaded; set_key skipped\n",
+				   sta->sta.addr);
 		goto out_unsupported;
+	}
 
 	if (sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) {
 		/*
@@ -178,9 +190,19 @@ static int ieee80211_key_enable_hw_accel(struct ieee80211_key *key)
 	    !(sdata->vif.active_links & BIT(key->conf.link_id)))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (test_early_upload)
+		sdata_info(sdata,
+			   "mac80211 FT key test: calling pre-ASSOC set_key (%d, %pM)\n",
+			   key->conf.keyidx, sta->sta.addr);
+
 	ret = drv_set_key(key->local, SET_KEY, sdata,
 			  sta ? &sta->sta : NULL, &key->conf);
 
+	if (test_early_upload)
+		sdata_info(sdata,
+			   "mac80211 FT key test: pre-ASSOC set_key (%d, %pM) returned %d\n",
+			   key->conf.keyidx, sta->sta.addr, ret);
+
 	if (!ret) {
 		key->flags |= KEY_FLAG_UPLOADED_TO_HARDWARE;
 
 		if (!(key->conf.flags & (IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_MMIC |
